         recommended test: pytest collects the same tests that acceptance check asked to run, with no mismatch between the requested test set and the collected test set.
           inputs:  Use a repository where pytest collection emits at least one collected test id to the plugin’s collected-file path, but the collection subprocess exits nonzero afterward (for example, a test module that collects successfully and then triggers a collection-time error in a later module). Invoke collect_tests/run collection with a requested id set that includes the collected test. The test must observe the collected file contents even when the subprocess return code is nonzero or the file read path is exercised after a failure.
           detects: The collection run can write collected ids to a file, but if pytest exits nonzero or the file is missing, the code falls back to an empty collected set instead of preserving the collected names it did obtain, so requested tests can be reported as unmatched even when pytest collected them.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion pytest-collected-tests-match-requested-tests

